// Option B (anomaly-gated metering, 2026-08-27): lightweight, APPROXIMATE
// aggregate telemetry for CLEAN/unflagged traffic — request counts, unique
// endpoint counts, error rate, and avg latency per alias-or-IP per time
// bucket. Intentionally NOT a billing-relevant table: it exists so B1/B10's
// population-level baseline needs (see DF-Session-task-report-27-08-26.md,
// Section 1) can still be fed without every clean request generating a full,
// billed LiveThreatEvent row. Rows are upsert-merged across batched SDK
// flushes (see TelemetryRollupBuffer), so counts are approximate under
// concurrent writes — acceptable here since this table is never read for
// billing/quota purposes.
model AliasTelemetryRollup {
